CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*interrupt_data)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct gasket_interrupt_data)...)
#200: FILE: drivers/staging/gasket/gasket_interrupt.c:331:
+	interrupt_data = kzalloc(sizeof(struct gasket_interrupt_data),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

